silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_01_foundational_thesis_and_anchors_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchors__anchor_g_the_source_directed_graph
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The substrate graph for the running Mittens domain. G_0 contains the individual cat Mittens, the class DomesticCat, the veterinary record VetRecord77, the body-mass quality BodyMassQuality77, the body-mass measurement BodyMassMeasurement99, the microchip identifier MicrochipIdentifier9, the nap-event NapEvent42, and the taxonomy row \"Felis catus / TSN 183798\". G_1 contains the typed edges rdf:type, is_about, bearer_of, measured_by, participates_in, has_microchip. " .

silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_01_foundational_thesis_and_anchors_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchors__anchor_a__b_arbitrary_nodes_%E2%80%94_abstract_math_notation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "A is the source object VetRecord77; B is the target object Mittens. The arrow s, t : G_1 -> G_0 reads: the source of the edge (v_record_77_is_about_mittens) is VetRecord77 and the target is Mittens. The reader entering with arbitrary \"A\" sees a concrete record-individual pair. " .

silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_01_foundational_thesis_and_anchors_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchors__anchor_p__q_paths_in_freeg
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "p is the path \"VetRecord77 -[is_about]-> Mittens -[rdf:type]-> DomesticCat\" (length 2). q is the direct edge \"VetRecord77 -> DomesticCat\" with label class_of_subject (if admitted). The shortcut q is admissible to C_G only as a NAMED composite, i.e. only when the equation q = (rdf:type) o (is_about) is defended. " .

silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_01_foundational_thesis_and_anchors_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchors__anchor_h__f__g_intermediate_functor___morphism
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "f is the typed arrow rdf:type : Mittens -> DomesticCat. g is the aboutness arrow is_about : VetRecord77 -> Mittens. The composite g; f is the typed path from VetRecord77 to DomesticCat that the shortcut may abbreviate, subject to a defended equation. " .

silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_01_foundational_thesis_and_anchors_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchors__anchor_d_mittensj_source_diagram_object_at_index_j
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The j-th source leg of the Mittens cocone. Examples: j=type yields DomesticCat (with arrow rdf:type); j=evidence yields VetRecord77 (with arrow is_about); j=taxonomy yields the taxonomy row \"Felis catus / TSN 183798\" (with the taxonomy arrow into D_Mittens); j=quality yields BodyMassQuality77 (with bearer_of); j=measurement yields BodyMassMeasurement99 (with measured_by); j=microchip yields MicrochipIdentifier9 (with has_microchip); j=process yields NapEvent42 (with participates_in). " .

silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_01_foundational_thesis_and_anchors_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchors__anchor_y_any_other_competing_cocone_target_%E2%80%94_abstract
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Y is the concrete competing cocone \"VetCarePlan22\" — the clinical summary that also receives the head-record and the torso-record legs along compatible arrows. The universal property gives a unique mediator u : Mittens -> VetCarePlan22 that names the clinical summary as a downstream profile target rather than as Mittens itself. " .

