silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_01_foundational_thesis_and_anchors_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchors
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GraphToCategoryGateConcreteAnchorsExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'GraphToCategoryGateConcreteAnchors', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, The substrate graph for the running Mittens domain. G_0 contains the individual cat Mittens, the class DomesticCat, the veterinary record VetRecord77, the body-mass quality BodyMassQuality77, the body-mass measurement BodyMassMeasurement99, the microchip identifier MicrochipIdentifier9, the nap-event NapEvent42, and the taxonomy row \"Felis catus / TSN 183798\". G_1 contains the typed edges rdf:type, is_about, bearer_of, measured_by, participates_in, has_microchip. ; also, A is the source object VetRecord77; B is the target object Mittens. The arrow s, t : G_1 -> G_0 reads: the source of the edge (v_record_77_is_about_mittens) is VetRecord77 and the target is Mittens. The reader entering with arbitrary \"A\" sees a concrete record-individual pair. ; also, p is the path \"VetRecord77 -[is_about]-> Mittens -[rdf:type]-> DomesticCat\" (length 2). q is the direct edge \"VetRecord77 -> DomesticCat\" with label class_of_subject (if admitted). The shortcut q is admissible to C_G only as a NAMED composite, i.e. only when the equation q = (rdf:type) o (is_about) is defended. ." .

