    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.10_graph_knowledge_graph_category.chapters.02_free_category_monad.sections.04_mittens_in_the_monad.concrete_anchors#u___mittens_->_vetcareplan22_is_the_unique_morphism_that_fac" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The u : Mittens -> VetCarePlan22 is the unique morphism that factors the care-plan cocone through Mittens. Its uniqueness says: the care plan derives FROM Mittens, and no other cat could play the role.  is u : Mittens -> VetCarePlan22 is the unique morphism that factors the care-plan cocone through Mittens. Its uniqueness says: the care plan derives FROM Mittens, and no other cat could play the role. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'u (unique mediator)', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_02_free_category_monad_sections_04_mittens_in_the_monad_concrete_anchors%23tg_is_the_underlying_graph_of_freeg%3B_it_has_no_composition__
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.10_graph_knowledge_graph_category.chapters.02_free_category_monad.sections.04_mittens_in_the_monad.concrete_anchors#tg_is_the_underlying_graph_of_freeg;_it_has_no_composition__" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The T(G) is the underlying graph of Free(G); it has no composition, so colimits don't exist there. G itself has no equation structure, so two paths to the same node need not be identifiable. Only after q : Free(G) -> C_G quotients by equiv_E does the colimit acquire universal force.  is T(G) is the underlying graph of Free(G); it has no composition, so colimits don't exist there. G itself has no equation structure, so two paths to the same node need not be identifiable. Only after q : Free(G) -> C_G quotients by equiv_E does the colimit acquire universal force." .

